DRAWNAPART (NDSS'22)
  Project: https://github.com/drawnapart/drawnapart
  Reference: T. Laor et al., "DRAWNAPART: A Device Identification
             Technique based on Remote GPU Fingerprinting,"
             NDSS 2022.
  Used by: baselines/drawnapart/

  The model definition in baselines/drawnapart/dp_keras_baseline.py and
  the matching layer list in dp_keras_to_torch.py (their get_clf_model
  and get_triplet_model: three Conv2D(128, 4x4, relu) /
  Dropout(0.119510) / AveragePooling2D blocks, Dense(256, relu),
  Dense(256), L2 normalization, softmax head) is taken from the authors'
  fpstalker_drawnapart.ipynb at commit bddd4f6, with the class count
  made a parameter, so that the baseline is their architecture rather
  than a reimplementation of it. The upstream repository carries no
  license file; the DRAWNAPART authors gave written permission (email,
  September 2026) to include and redistribute their code in this
  artifact, on the condition that a link to their repository and full
  attribution to their paper appear in the header of every bundled
  file. Those headers are on dp_keras_baseline.py, dp_keras_to_torch.py
  and released_model.py; the code is not covered by the artifact's MIT
  License. Their collector is not
  included; baselines/drawnapart/README.md points to it upstream and
  documents the trace layout this code reads. Everything else under
  baselines/drawnapart/ (training driver, scaler, weight conversion and
  its check, data loading, evaluation pipeline, launcher, CLI, configs,
  the torch port) is original and MIT-licensed with the rest of the
  artifact.

